xian","#Coccato","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html",{"type":45,"ref":46,"location":49},"provenance",{"_":47,"target":48},"Tyros, Greece","https://www.geonames.org/256631/nisi-naxos.html",{"geo":50},"37.07257,25.48616","",{"layout":53},{"p":54,"rs":55,"damage":51},"The Latin text is engraved over two lines (letters c.20 mm high, but of uneven height), to a maximum length of 52 cm.",{"_":56,"ana":57,"ref":58},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":60,"dimensions":61}," The letters show some irregularity, with fairly pronounced serifs, and lengthy tails to the letter R. The first two words are separated from the rest by a space; an interpunct is visible at the end of the dedicant’s name, and the final abbreviated phrase is separated from the rest by a large hedera (ivy leaf). The letter I in line 1 is frequently taller than the rest (but so too is the first L in line 1); the final I of line 1 is somewhat irregularly carved.",[62,70,76],{"type":63,"l":64,"from":65,"to":65,"h":66,"unit":67,"atLeast":68,"atMost":69},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","18-25","mm","18","25",{"type":63,"l":71,"from":72,"to":72,"h":73,"unit":67,"atLeast":74,"atMost":75},"Line 2","line2","19-23","19","23",{"type":77,"l":78,"from":65,"to":72,"h":79,"unit":67,"atLeast":80,"atMost":81},"interlinear","Interlineation lines 1-2","7-15","7","15",{"_":83,"notBefore":84,"notAfter":85,"evidence":86},"Statue can be dated stylistically to the late Antonine period (i.e. the 180s or 190s CE), and the text is compatible with such a date.",180,199,"context",[88,93],{"_":89,"type":90,"ref":91,"region":92},"Halaesa","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462225","Sicilia",{"_":94,"type":95,"ref":96,"offset":97,"region":92},"Castel di Tusa","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/2525099","near",[99],[100,101],37.99907,14.26197,[103,104],37.998037,14.262643,"Sicily",{"_":107,"role":108,"ref":109},"Antiquarium e sito archeologico di Halaesa 